$ goodfetch-foxhound --help
Foxhound, Goodfetch's Product for crawling, which contains Collie.

Usage: goodfetch-foxhound [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  browser          Manages the browser builds this version pins in the Browser cache
  audit            Exports and verifies the user's Audit log
  certs            Lists, accepts and forgets the certificate pins of the user's known-certificates store
  config           Shows the settings and where each value comes from
  daemon           Starts, stops and shows the Daemon of this executable's major, which both Products share
  runs             Works on the runs of this executable's major, of both Products
  usage            Shows, sets and raises the Limits of the user's Usage ledger, which hold every engine of the user
  upgrade-files    Gives this executable's major its own copy of an older major's settings, Operator policy, Run index and runs in Goodfetch home, never changing the older major's files
  engine           Calls the catalog's `engine` operations
  events           Calls the catalog's `events` operations
  needs-you        Calls the catalog's `needs_you` operations
  run              Calls the catalog's `run` operations
  session          Calls the catalog's `session` operations
  page             Calls the catalog's `page` operations
  locator          Calls the catalog's `locator` operations
  response         Calls the catalog's `response` operations
  signing-key      Calls the catalog's `signing_key` operations
  key-value-store  Calls the catalog's `key_value_store` operations
  sample           Calls the catalog's `sample` operations
  crawl            Calls the catalog's `crawl` operations
  dataset          Calls the catalog's `dataset` operations

Options:
      --color <WHEN>  When to colour human output; `auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set and not empty [default: auto] [possible values: auto, always, never]
  -h, --help          Print help

