$ goodfetch-foxhound usage --help
Shows, sets and raises the Limits of the user's Usage ledger, which hold every engine of the user

Usage: goodfetch-foxhound usage [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  list   Lists every Limit of the Usage ledger, by scope, with the Usage charged and held against it in its current period and what is left
  set    Adds a Limit of the caller's own to the Usage ledger, which holds beside the others: the tightest one holds, so it can only lower what applies. Answers it with its Usage
  raise  Raises a Limit, in place of the ones of its scope, Usage kind, currency and period but a managed Operator policy's: a person's answer, asked at the terminal, and refused with `person_required` when stdin is no terminal

Options:
      --color <WHEN>  When to colour human output; `auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set and not empty [default: auto] [possible values: auto, always, never]
  -h, --help          Print help

$ goodfetch-foxhound usage list --help
Lists every Limit of the Usage ledger, by scope, with the Usage charged and held against it in its current period and what is left

Usage: goodfetch-foxhound usage list [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --json          Prints the result as JSON
      --attached      Runs the call on an Attached engine in this process, even when a Daemon runs
      --daemon        Runs the call on the Daemon of the major, starting it if none runs; its refusal ends the command
      --color <WHEN>  When to colour human output; `auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set and not empty [default: auto] [possible values: auto, always, never]
  -h, --help          Print help

$ goodfetch-foxhound usage set --help
Adds a Limit of the caller's own to the Usage ledger, which holds beside the others: the tightest one holds, so it can only lower what applies. Answers it with its Usage

Usage: goodfetch-foxhound usage set [OPTIONS] --amount <AMOUNT> --scope <SCOPE> --usage-kind <USAGE_KIND>

Options:
      --amount <AMOUNT>          How much it allows per period: a count of the Usage kind, or millionths of the currency
      --currency <CURRENCY>      The currency it caps the price in, an ISO 4217 code
      --period <PERIOD>          The period it counts over; none for a Limit that never starts again
      --scope <SCOPE>            The scope's kind
      --scope-id <SCOPE_ID>      Which one of its kind; the caller's own when absent (its Client connection, its person, the engine's Daemon, the install)
      --usage-kind <USAGE_KIND>  The Usage kind it caps
      --color <WHEN>             When to colour human output; `auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set and not empty [default: auto] [possible values: auto, always, never]
      --json                     Prints the result as JSON
      --attached                 Runs the call on an Attached engine in this process, even when a Daemon runs
      --daemon                   Runs the call on the Daemon of the major, starting it if none runs; its refusal ends the command
  -h, --help                     Print help

$ goodfetch-foxhound usage raise --help
Raises a Limit, in place of the ones of its scope, Usage kind, currency and period but a managed Operator policy's: a person's answer, asked at the terminal, and refused with `person_required` when stdin is no terminal

Usage: goodfetch-foxhound usage raise [OPTIONS] --scope <SCOPE> --usage-kind <USAGE_KIND> --amount <AMOUNT>

Options:
