      --scope-id <SCOPE_ID>      Which one of its kind; the person's own when absent
      --usage-kind <USAGE_KIND>  The Usage kind it caps
      --currency <CURRENCY>      The currency it caps the price in, an ISO 4217 code
      --period <PERIOD>          The period it counts over, as JSON such as `{"every":"month","time_zone":"UTC"}`; none for a Limit that never starts again
      --amount <AMOUNT>          How much it allows per period from now on: a count of the Usage kind, or millionths of the currency
      --attached                 Runs the call on an Attached engine in this process, even when a Daemon runs
      --color <WHEN>             When to colour human output; `auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set and not empty [default: auto] [possible values: auto, always, never]
      --daemon                   Runs the call on the Daemon of the major, starting it if none runs; its refusal ends the command
